## Count the totals of 7 and of 11
In the completed table there are 36 equally likely outcomes. A total of 7 appears 6 times and a total of 11 appears 2 times.
## Divide favourable outcomes by 36
P(7 \text{ or } 11) &= \frac{6+2}{36}
&= \frac{8}{36}
&= \frac{2}{9}
ANSWER: \frac{2}{9}

## Count the totals that are prime numbers
The primes up to 12 are 2, 3, 5, 7 and 11. Their counts in the table are 1, 2, 4, 6 and 2.
## Divide favourable outcomes by 36
P(\text{prime}) &= \frac{1+2+4+6+2}{36}
&= \frac{15}{36}
&= \frac{5}{12}
ANSWER: \frac{5}{12}

## Find the cars that are not counted
A car fails "Ford or not red" only if it is a Renault that is red. There are 4 of these.
## Subtract them from the total
P(\text{Ford or not red}) &= \frac{30-4}{30}
&= \frac{26}{30}
&= \frac{13}{15}
ANSWER: \frac{13}{15}

## Find the slope of UV
$U(4, 6)$ and $V(9, 7)$.
m_{UV} &= \frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}
&= \frac{7-6}{9-4}
&= \frac{1}{5}
## Find the slope of QR
$Q(1, 2)$ and $R(11, 4)$.
m_{QR} &= \frac{4-2}{11-1}
&= \frac{2}{10}
&= \frac{1}{5}
## Compare the slopes
Both slopes equal $\frac{1}{5}$, so $UV$ and $QR$ are parallel.
ANSWER: UV \parallel QR

## (i) Find each probability
The spinner is unbiased, so each probability is the sector angle divided by the full turn, $360^\circ$.
P(\text{red}) &= \frac{72}{360}
&= \frac{1}{5}
P(\text{orange}) &= \frac{30}{360}
&= \frac{1}{12}
P(\text{yellow}) &= \frac{45}{360}
&= \frac{1}{8}
P(\text{green}) &= \frac{90}{360}
&= \frac{1}{4}
P(\text{blue}) &= \frac{60}{360}
&= \frac{1}{6}
P(\text{indigo}) &= \frac{18}{360}
&= \frac{1}{20}
P(\text{violet}) &= \frac{45}{360}
&= \frac{1}{8}
## (ii) Multiply each prize by its probability
The expected value is the sum of (prize $\times$ probability).
E(X) &= 20\left(\frac{1}{5}\right) + 60\left(\frac{1}{12}\right) + 24\left(\frac{1}{8}\right) + 8\left(\frac{1}{4}\right) + 42\left(\frac{1}{6}\right) + 90\left(\frac{1}{20}\right) + 48\left(\frac{1}{8}\right)
&= 4 + 5 + 3 + 2 + 7 + 4.5 + 6
&= 31.5
ANSWER: \text{€}31.50

## Find the distance from the centre (5, 4) to B(9, 0)
r &= \sqrt{(x_2-x_1)^2 + (y_2-y_1)^2}
&= \sqrt{(9-5)^2 + (0-4)^2}
&= \sqrt{4^2 + (-4)^2}
&= \sqrt{16 + 16}
&= \sqrt{32}
## Write the surd as p times the square root of q
\sqrt{32} &= \sqrt{16 \times 2}
&= \sqrt{16}\,\sqrt{2}
&= 4\sqrt{2}
ANSWER: 4\sqrt{2}
